From 4e65a098ac6fc7baab320b8effda08457771ddf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:54:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: mt6397: stop initialization on interrupt-mask failure

Do not create an IRQ domain or register the parent handler when an
initial interrupt-mask write fails. Propagate the bus error and name the
failed bank. Previously initialization ignored the failure and proceeded
with an unproved hardware mask state.

Earlier banks may already have been masked when a later write fails;
this change performs no retry or restoration of unknown state.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/mfd/mt6397-irq.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mt6397-irq.c b/drivers/mfd/mt6397-irq.c
index a21e041..fe2391d 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/mt6397-irq.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mt6397-irq.c
@@ -220,8 +220,12 @@ int mt6397_irq_init(struct mt6397_chip *chip)
 	}
 
 	/* Mask all interrupt sources */
-	for (i = 0; i < chip->num_irq_regs; i++)
-		regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->int_con[i], 0x0);
+	for (i = 0; i < chip->num_irq_regs; i++) {
+		ret = regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->int_con[i], 0x0);
+		if (ret)
+			return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, ret,
+					     "Failed to mask interrupt bank %u\n", i);
+	}
 
 	chip->pm_nb.notifier_call = mt6397_irq_pm_notifier;
 	chip->irq_domain = irq_domain_create_linear(dev_fwnode(chip->dev),
